  "title": "15 February 1964: The Beatles in Miami",
  "date": "1964-02-15",
  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p>The day before their second appearance on The Ed Sullivan Show, The Beatles spent all afternoon rehearsing at their Miami hotel. <span id=\"more-2405\"></span></p><p>The group rehearsed at the Deauville Hotel’s Napoleon Room; George Harrison and Ringo Starr wore shirts and swimming trunks. At 2pm there was a dress rehearsal before an audience of 2,500 people, the majority of whom had been queuing outside the hotel since early in the morning.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/02/15/rehearsal-ed-sullivan-show-3/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-2405 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01/\"><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"181\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01-181x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Beatles rehearsing for their second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01-181x200.jpg 181w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01-525x580.jpg 525w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01-768x848.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01.jpg 851w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 181px) 100vw, 181px\" data-attachment-id=\"27620\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"851,940\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-ti