=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_07-637x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzciIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM3IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"137\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08-137x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Beatles rehearsing for their second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08-137x200.jpg 137w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08-398x580.jpg 398w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08-659x960.jpg 659w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08-768x1119.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08.jpg 800w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 137px) 100vw, 137px\" data-attachment-id=\"27627\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"800,1166\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Beatles rehearsing for their second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_08-659x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMDYiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTA2IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"106\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09-106x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr rehearsing for The Beatles' second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09-106x200.jpg 106w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09-306x580.jpg 306w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09-507x960.jpg 507w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09-768x1454.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09.jpg 800w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 106px) 100vw, 106px\" data-attachment-id=\"27628\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"800,1515\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr rehearsing for The Beatles&amp;#8217; second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_09-507x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzciIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM3IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"137\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10-137x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Beatles rehearsing for their second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10-137x200.jpg 137w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10-398x580.jpg 398w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10-658x960.jpg 658w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10-768x1120.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10.jpg 800w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 137px) 100vw, 137px\" data-attachment-id=\"27629\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"800,1167\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Beatles rehearsing for their second Ed Sullivan Show, 15 February 1964\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640215-beatles-ed-sullivan-rehearsal_10-658x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>After the rehearsals were complete The Beatles went fishing.</p><blockquote><div>I think, though, we were hanging out with Mafiosi at that time. There was a critic giving us a hard time in the press; <a href=\"/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a> and <a href=\"/people/brian-epstein/\">Brian Epstein</a> were discussing it when a big heavy guy came up and said, ‘Mr Epstein, you want we should fix this guy?’ – ‘Er, no, that’s OK.’ That was the kind of crowd we were in: ‘Yeah, I’m in the Mafia.’ But <em>we</em> didn’t know that: we just saw a nice man with a pool and a yacht. I must admit we were more interested in the yacht than in him.<p></p><p>At this stage, we started to meet people whom we’d only seen in newspapers and on film, and now we were rubbing shoulders with them.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>Also on this day, a telephone interview with The Beatles was broadcast on Dick Clark’s influential ABC-TV series American Bandstand. The half-hour show was broadcast from 12.30pm EST.</p>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 13 February 2017</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2024: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2024/02/15/paul-mccartneys-first-hofner-bass-returned-after-five-decades/\">Paul McCartney’s first Höfner bass returned after five decades</a></li><li>2016: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2016/02/15/paul-mccartney-announces-first-live-shows-2016/\">Paul McCartney announces first live shows of 2016</a></li><li>2015: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2015/02/15/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-bjcc-concert-hall-birmingham/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: BJCC Concert Hall, Birmingham</a></li><li>2015: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2015/02/15/paul-mccartney-saturday-night-live-40th-anniversary-special/\">Paul McCartney performs on Saturday Night Live 40th anniversary special</a></li><li>2010: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2010/02/15/revolver-tops-vatican-best-albums-list/\">The Beatles’ Revolver tops the Vatican’s best albums list</a></li><li>1990: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1990/02/15/paul-mccartney-live-market-square-arena-indianapolis-2/\">Paul McCartney live: Market Square Arena, Indianapolis</a></li><li>1977: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1977/02/15/recording-children-children-wings/\">Recording: Children Children by Wings</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/02/15/recording-mixing-born-in-a-prison-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">Recording, mixing: Born In A Prison by John Lennon and Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/02/15/recording-mixing-maybe-im-amazed-by-paul-mccartney/\">Recording, mixing: Maybe I’m Amazed by Paul McCartney</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/02/15/mixing-lady-madonna/\">Mixing: Lady Madonna</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/02/15/john-lennon-and-george-harrison-fly-to-india/\">John Lennon and George Harrison fly to India</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/02/15/recording-ticket-to-ride-another-girl-i-need-you/\">Recording: Ticket To Ride, Another Girl, I Need You</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/02/15/john-lennon-passes-driving-test/\">John Lennon passes his driving test</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/02/15/us-single-eight-days-a-week/\">US single release: Eight Days A Week</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/02/15/live-ritz-ballroom-birmingham/\">The Beatles live: Ritz Ballroom, Birmingham</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/02/15/live-tower-ballroom-new-brighton-wallasey-10/\">The Beatles live: Tower Ballroom, New Brighton, Wallasey</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/02/15/live-cavern-club-liverpool-136/\">The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/02/15/live-hambleton-hall-liverpool-4/\">The Beatles live: Hambleton Hall, Liverpool</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/02/15/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-10/\">The Beatles live: Aintree Institute, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=697454a64f5900909e4b8e770a149a1b&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=2405&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "The day before their second appearance on The Ed Sullivan Show, The Beatles spent all afternoon rehearsing at their Miami hotel. The group rehearsed at the Deauville Hotel’s Napoleon Room; George Harrison and Ringo Starr wore shirts and swimming trunks. At 2pm there was a dress rehearsal before an audience of 2,500 people, the majority of whom had been queuing outside the hotel since early in the morning.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAfter the rehearsals were complete The Beatles went fishing.I think, though, we were hanging out with Mafiosi at that time. There was a critic giving us a hard time in the press; George Martin and Brian Epstein were discussing it when a big heavy guy came up and said, ‘Mr Epstein, you want we should fix this guy?’ – ‘Er, no, that’s OK.’ That was the kind of crowd we were in: ‘Yeah, I’m in the Mafia.’ But we didn’t know that: we just saw a nice man with a pool and a yacht. I must admit we were more interested in the yacht than in him.At this stage, we started to meet people whom we’d only seen in newspapers and on film, and now we were rubbing shoulders with them.Paul McCartney\nAnthologyAlso on this day, a telephone interview with The Beatles was broadcast on Dick Clark’s influential ABC-TV series American Bandstand. The half-hour show was broadcast from 12.30pm EST.\nPage last updated: 13 February 2017Also on this day...2024: Paul McCartney’s first Höfner bass returned after five decades2016: Paul McCartney announces first live shows of 20162015: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: BJCC Concert Hall, Birmingham2015: Paul McCartney performs on Saturday Night Live 40th anniversary special2010: The Beatles’ Revolver tops the Vatican’s best albums list1990: Paul McCartney live: Market Square Arena, Indianapolis1977: Recording: Children Children by Wings1972: Recording, mixing: Born In A Prison by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1970: Recording, mixing: Maybe I’m Amazed by Paul McCartney1968: Mixing: Lady Madonna1968: John Lennon and George Harrison fly to India1965: Recording: Ticket To Ride, Another Girl, I Need You1965: John Lennon passes his driving test1965: US single release: Eight Days A Week1963: The Beatles live: Ritz Ballroom, Birmingham1962: The Beatles live: Tower Ballroom, New Brighton, Wallasey1962: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)1961: The Beatles live: Hambleton Hall, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Aintree Institute, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
